b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), recursive procedures and function designators with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), Boolean procedures and the Boolean operator of negation (3.4), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: L1 L2 s1 ... sL1 t1 ... tL2, the two lengths, and then the elements of the known sequences s1 and s2 of setdiff(s1, s2, d). Elements are integers, an atom being its integer code;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P06d. setdiff(s1, s2, d) with s1 and s2 known: d is computed from them by the cases of setdiff, in order, as a function, the direction this query uses, and mem is a Boolean procedure that tests mem(e, s) with both known, by its cases in order. Case 3 of setdiff tests its own conjunct not mem(h, s2) with the negation of the language. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence hd[c] followed by the sequence tl[c];
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, l1, l2;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants: the two lengths, which size the cells, and then the elements;
  l1 := read; l2 := read;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ top, s1, s2, d, mem1, mem2, sd1, sd2, sd3;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl[1:l1 + l1 + l2 + 1];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence h followed by the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ readseq(len);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ len; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ len;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a sequence of len elements, read from the input in order;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, e, first, last, c;
    first := last := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ len d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      e := read; c := cons(e, 0);
      i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := c e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := c;
      last := c
    e̲n̲d̲;
    readseq := first
  e̲n̲d̲ readseq;

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ mem(e, s);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ e, s; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ e, s;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ mem(e, s), tested by its cases, in order. Case 1: mem(e, the sequence e followed by t), for every sequence t. Case 2: mem(e, the sequence h followed by t) if mem(e, t). The empty sequence matches neither head;
  i̲f̲ s = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ mem := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ hd[s] = e t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ mem1 := mem1 + 1; mem := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ mem2 := mem2 + 1; mem := mem(e, tl[s]) e̲n̲d̲ mem;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ setdiff(s, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ s, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ s, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ setdiff(s, t, d), computing d from s and t by its cases, in order. Case 1: setdiff(the empty sequence, t, the empty sequence). Case 2: setdiff(h followed by r, t, d) if mem(h, t) and setdiff(r, t, d). Case 3: setdiff(h followed by r, t, h followed by d) if not mem(h, t) and setdiff(r, t, d);
  i̲f̲ s = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ sd1 := sd1 + 1; setdiff := 0 e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ mem(hd[s], t) t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ sd2 := sd2 + 1; setdiff := setdiff(tl[s], t) e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ¬mem(hd[s], t) t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ r;
    sd3 := sd3 + 1;
    r := setdiff(tl[s], t);
    setdiff := cons(hd[s], r)
  e̲n̲d̲ setdiff;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(p);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence, its elements in parentheses, separated by commas;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ p ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ print(hd[p]); p := tl[p]; i̲f̲ p ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ') e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

  top := mem1 := mem2 := sd1 := sd2 := sd3 := 0;
  s1 := readseq(l1);
  s2 := readseq(l2);

  d := setdiff(s1, s2);

  PRINTTEXT(`[answer]d = '); printseq(d); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations setdiff/1 '); print(sd1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations setdiff/2 '); print(sd2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations setdiff/3 '); print(sd3); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations mem/1 '); print(mem1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations mem/2 '); print(mem2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
